# Cloudflare Pages headers. F5: defence in depth, so a future HTML-injection mistake
# degrades to a broken element rather than a stolen responder token.
#
# NOTE: this file is currently INERT. The site is served by GitHub Pages, which does
# not read `_headers`, and `ingest.yml` only copies web/*.html and web/*.js into the
# deployed site. It is kept accurate anyway, because the day this moves back behind
# Cloudflare a stale CSP would silently break whatever it forgot to allow. The
# kinesisvideo and execute-api entries are the Yala camera streams: `media-src` had
# to be named explicitly because it otherwise falls back to `default-src 'self'`,
# which forbids video outright. Hat Yai is a still rather than a stream, so it
# needs `img-src` (to show the photo) and `connect-src` (to read the camera list),
# and deliberately NOT `media-src`.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://unpkg.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://unpkg.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://basemaps.cartocdn.com https://*.basemaps.cartocdn.com https://hatyaicityclimate.org; media-src 'self' blob: https://*.kinesisvideo.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com; connect-src 'self' https://basemaps.cartocdn.com https://*.basemaps.cartocdn.com https://api-v3.thaiwater.net https://gg89f6g289.execute-api.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com https://*.kinesisvideo.ap-southeast-1.amazonaws.com https://hatyaicityclimate.org; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), geolocation=(self)
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# config.js carries the deployment endpoints. Never cache it hard, or changing an
# endpoint leaves visitors pinned to the old one until their cache expires.
/config.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
